DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ttookkeennaaddmm utility displays and edits user entries in the various token
     databases.  It may also be invoked as one the following: aaccttiivvaaddmm,
     ccrryyppttooaaddmm, or ssnnkkaaddmm.

     The options are as follows:

     --11      Display users, one per line.

     --BB      Display users with no banner.

     --DD      Display disabled users.

     --dd      Disable users without removing them from the database.  This pre‐
             vents the users from authenticating, but does not lose their
             shared secret.  The --mm flag may also be used with the --dd flag.

     --EE      Display enabled users.

     --ee      Enable users.  This should be used to re-enable users who were
             disabled by the --dd flag.  The --mm flag may also be used with the
             --ee flag.

     --mm [-]_m_o_d_e
             Add [or remove] the specified mode of authentication for the
             user.  Modes available are decimal (dec), hexadecimal (hex),
             phonebook (phone), and reduced-input (rim).  Not all modes are
             available for all types of cards.  The --mm flag may be used alone
             or in conjunction with either the --dd or --ee flags.  Whenever re‐
             duced-input mode is set, the reduced-input state is reset.  This
             should be done if a paper copy of challenge/responses had been
             produced and then misplaced.

     --RR      Display users in reverse order.

     --rr      Remove users from the database.

     --TT      Display users in terse format (only the user names).  Unless --11
             is also specified, four users will be displayed per line.

     Use of any of the --11BBDDEERRTT flags precludes the use of any of the --ddeemmrr
     flags.  The --ddeemmrr flags all require at least one _u_s_e_r argument.

